  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38137534",
      "title": "An Alternative Way Of Creating Reducers",
      "lectureOrder": 689,
      "videoOrder": 634,
      "sourceHash": "bf5e1735a952a7d8bd2584f0d91f59918441d0468a3aa9c54c6768cff65b5537",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 4.11,
          "en": "Now, as you saw in the previous lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.11,
          "end": 7.11,
          "en": "creating a Reducer is quite simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.11,
          "end": 10.44,
          "en": "You just have to execute the createReducer function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.44,
          "end": 13.443,
          "en": "which is provided by NgRx Store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.43,
          "end": 15.9,
          "en": "Now, it can be interesting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.9,
          "end": 18.57,
          "en": "to take a look under the hood here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.57,
          "end": 21.81,
          "en": "Also, because later in this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.81,
          "end": 24.72,
          "en": "I will be using a slightly different way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.72,
          "end": 27.18,
          "en": "of creating these Reducers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.18,
          "end": 30.63,
          "en": "also to help you understand what's going on under the hood",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.63,
          "end": 33.93,
          "en": "and also because this createReducer function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.93,
          "end": 36.75,
          "en": "has been around for quite some time now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.75,
          "end": 40.71,
          "en": "but is not supported in older versions of NgRx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.71,
          "end": 42.84,
          "en": "And, if you're therefore working on projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.84,
          "end": 45.93,
          "en": "that do use older versions of NgRx",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.93,
          "end": 49.26,
          "en": "because they might be using older versions of Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.26,
          "end": 50.91,
          "en": "which is not uncommon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.91,
          "end": 53.37,
          "en": "you should know the alternative way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.37,
          "end": 55.5,
          "en": "of creating such Reducers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.5,
          "end": 58.77,
          "en": "which, in the end, is used under the hood by createReducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.77,
          "end": 60.54,
          "en": "and which will always work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.54,
          "end": 63.603,
          "en": "no matter which NgRx version you're using.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.83,
          "end": 66.66,
          "en": "And, when using this older",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.66,
          "end": 69.6,
          "en": "or simply alternative approach here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.6,
          "end": 73.53,
          "en": "you would create the Reducer function yourself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.53,
          "end": 75.93,
          "en": "counterReducer could still be the name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.93,
          "end": 79.14,
          "en": "And you would still export it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.14,
          "end": 81.72,
          "en": "Now, this counterReducer function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.72,
          "end": 82.95,
          "en": "which we're creating here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 82.95,
          "end": 86.16,
          "en": "should always accept at least one value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.16,
          "end": 89.22,
          "en": "And that one argument that should be accepted, at least,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.22,
          "end": 94.11,
          "en": "should be the current State that's being managed by NgRx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.11,
          "end": 97.65,
          "en": "Because counterReducer, this Reducer function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.65,
          "end": 101.25,
          "en": "will later be executed by NgRx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.25,
          "end": 106.25,
          "en": "and NgRx will, for example, execute this Reducer function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.35,
          "end": 109.05,
          "en": "whenever an Action occurs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.05,
          "end": 113.00999999999999,
          "en": "or also when it initially sets up the Store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.00999999999999,
          "end": 116.34,
          "en": "And that's, by the way, exactly the same for the Reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.34,
          "end": 118.97999999999999,
          "en": "that was created with createReducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.97999999999999,
          "end": 120.21,
          "en": "This Reducer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 120.21,
          "end": 123.6,
          "en": "which also is simply such a function under the hood,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.6,
          "end": 127.47,
          "en": "will be executed by NgRx when an Action occurs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.47,
          "end": 130.5,
          "en": "or when the Store is being set up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.5,
          "end": 133.83,
          "en": "Now, when this function is then executed by NgRx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 133.83,
          "end": 138.51,
          "en": "it expects that you then return the updated new State.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.51,
          "end": 141.42000000000002,
          "en": "And, therefore, here, for this very basic use case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.42000000000002,
          "end": 145.29,
          "en": "we might wanna return the initialState here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 145.29,
          "end": 147.66,
          "en": "So we could set up our Reducer like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.66,
          "end": 150.24,
          "en": "Though it's actually recommended that you, instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.24,
          "end": 154.05,
          "en": "set your initialState as a default value for this argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.05,
          "end": 157.38,
          "en": "so that, if this Reducer function should be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.38,
          "end": 160.11,
          "en": "without a State being passed into it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.11,
          "end": 162.18,
          "en": "which is exactly what will be the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162.18,
          "end": 165.3,
          "en": "when the Store is created for the first time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 165.3,
          "end": 167.43,
          "en": "because, at that point of time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 167.43,
          "end": 170.43,
          "en": "no State values will exist yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.43,
          "end": 173.04,
          "en": "So, when that's the case, the initialState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 173.04,
          "end": 176.25,
          "en": "will be passed in as a argument by NgRx instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 176.25,
          "end": 179.25,
          "en": "and you can then simply return the current state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 179.25,
          "end": 182.13,
          "en": "as a default value in this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 182.13,
          "end": 184.35,
          "en": "So, with that, counterReducer here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 184.35,
          "end": 186.48,
          "en": "will always return the current State.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 186.48,
          "end": 189.6,
          "en": "And, initially, when it's being executed the first time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 189.6,
          "end": 191.19,
          "en": "and there is no State yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 191.19,
          "end": 194.403,
          "en": "the State will simply be set to this initialState here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 195.48,
          "end": 198.21,
          "en": "So, when you could also create your Reducer like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198.21,
          "end": 200.34,
          "en": "and that's, in the end, what's happening here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 200.34,
          "end": 203.13,
          "en": "when using createReducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 203.13,
          "end": 205.74,
          "en": "And, of course, for this very simple Reducer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 205.74,
          "end": 208.65,
          "en": "which doesn't contain any extra logic yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 208.65,
          "end": 211.41,
          "en": "both approaches look quite similar,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 211.41,
          "end": 214.32,
          "en": "you will see more differences a little bit later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 214.32,
          "end": 218.49,
          "en": "once we start adding some logic to the Reducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 218.49,
          "end": 220.26,
          "en": "But, for the moment, that's it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 220.26,
          "end": 221.67000000000002,
          "en": "And you can, of course, therefore use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 221.67000000000002,
          "end": 224.73,
          "en": "exactly the same approach in this application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 224.73,
          "end": 226.92000000000002,
          "en": "that uses Standalone Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 226.92000000000002,
          "end": 230.07,
          "en": "You could also create your Reducer like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 230.07,
          "end": 232.59,
          "en": "and it would then still be mapped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 232.59,
          "end": 235.07999999999998,
          "en": "to that key of your choice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 235.07999999999998,
          "end": 238.53,
          "en": "in the place where the Store is being created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 238.53,
          "end": 241.35,
          "en": "So, therefore, over here in this NgModule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 241.35,
          "end": 243.93,
          "en": "to register this Reducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 243.93,
          "end": 245.46,
          "en": "And then, as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 245.46,
          "end": 249.24,
          "en": "this Reducer function will be executed by NgRx",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 249.24,
          "end": 251.88,
          "en": "when it first creates that Store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 251.88,
          "end": 254.79,
          "en": "But that's, of course, not the only point of time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 254.79,
          "end": 257.433,
          "en": "where this Reducer will be executed.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
